<title>USA: N.Y. business loans rose $869 mln in July 2 week.</title>
<headline>N.Y. business loans rose $869 mln in July 2 week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commercial and industrial loans at the six major New York banks, excluding acceptances, rose $869 million to $46,468 million in the week ended July 2, the Federal Reserve Bank of New York said.</p>
<p>Including acceptances, loans rose $870 million to $46,740 million.</p>
<p>Commercial paper outstanding nationally fell $2,465 million to $869,436 million.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
